  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best rna_only config (config_005: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) achieves 0.650 acc, while the only multimodal test (config_030: same RNA settings + resnet50, concat fusion) scores 0.632 — slightly worse. Image-only (config_010) is very weak (0.208), suggesting resnet50 features may be noisy or uninformative. The key uncertainty is whether the small multimodal deficit is due to the concat fusion failing to handle modality imbalance, or whether the resnet50 image features are simply unhelpful. This experiment (config_031) changes only the fusion from concat to weighted, holding all other settings identical to config_030. If weighted fusion recovers the gap to ~0.650+, it shows the image carries marginal signal that concat was diluting; if it does not, it strongly indicates the resnet50 image features are not useful and we should pivot to testing a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) or focus further on RNA-only improvements. This single-variable comparison is the most efficient way to isolate the fusion effect before committing further budget to multimodal variants."
}

